    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="d259-01" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve05p1/d259-01"/>

                <head>260. Telegram 179228 From the Department of State to the Embassy in
                        Uganda<anchor n="1" xml:id="d260-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d260-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date calendar="gregorian" when="1972-09-30T18:38:00+00:00">September 30, 1972,
                        1838Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <pb facs="d260-01" n="1" xml:id="d260-01"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Admission Stateless Asians on Parole</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Attorney General, in reply to Secretaryʼs request, has found it would be in
                    public interest to grant parole to stateless Ugandan Asians and has authorized
                    under Section 212 (D) (5) of Immigration and Nationality Act the parole into US
                    of up to 1,000 stateless Ugandan Asians.</p>
                <p>2. Dept planning make public announcement October 2. Nothing should be said about
                    decision until you informed release made here. Our announcement will seek to
                    emphasize fact that up to 1,000 well qualified individuals rather than faceless
                    block of persons will be paroled.</p>
                <p>3. Dept has informed UK Embassy Washington.</p>
                <p>4. For USUN—you requested notify Senator McGee.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 23–10 Uganda.
                    Limited Official Use; Immediate. Repeated Immediate to London, Nairobi, Dar es
                    Salaam, Addis Ababa, Geneva, Islamabad, New Delhi, Dacca, and USUN.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f2" n="2" xml:id="d260-f2-content">
                <p>The Department informed the Embassy that up to 1,000 stateless Ugandan Asians
                    would be paroled into the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
